{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00694 - MONDO_18434",
  "verbalization": "Daunorubicin is associated with Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) through a shared indication with Glasdegib, which in turn is linked to AML with T(9;11)(p22;q23). This suggests a potential pathway where Daunorubicin may exert its therapeutic effect through a mechanism that is also active in AML with this chromosomal translocation. The presence of Glasdegib in both the Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia With Maturation and Without Maturation subtypes indicates that Glasdegib may act as a common mediator in the progression of AML, possibly through targeting specific molecular pathways. The integration of Daunorubicin into this pathway implies that it may share a mechanism of action with Glasdegib, potentially through a common target or pathway, which could explain its association with AML with T(9;11)(p22;q23). The evidence supports a possible role for Daunorubicin in AML with this specific chromosomal abnormality, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
